If person don dey feel low or somehow for long time, dey avoid people, and e no dey act like im normal self, e fit don pass ordinary bad mood, especially if e dey affect daily life.

Signs wey show say professional help fit be important include:

low mood, hopelessness, anger, or sadness wey last about two weeks or more;
person no dey enjoy things wey e normally like before;
e dey avoid family, friends, work, school, or normal activities;
sleep, appetite, energy, or concentration don change well well;
e dey struggle to do normal daily things or take care of imself;
e dey talk say e feel useless, guilty, helpless, or say nothing go better;
e dey use alcohol or drugs more to cope;
the problem dey get worse instead of better.

Person no need wait until the matter become very serious before e seek help. Doctor or trained mental-health professional fit assess wetin dey happen, check whether another health problem fit dey involved, and discuss treatment or support like counselling, therapy, or medicine if needed.

If the person talk say e wan die, harm imself, or say everybody go better without am, or e no fit keep imself safe, treat am as urgent. Stay with the person if possible and get emergency or urgent mental-health help immediately.

Best support from family or friends na to listen without judging, take the person seriously, and encourage am to get professional help instead of telling am to just “cheer up” or manage am alone.

If person don dey feel low for long time, dey avoid people, and e no dey act like im normal self again, e fit don pass ordinary bad mood, especially if the change dey affect how e dey live day to day.

Signs wey show say e need professional help include:

sadness, hopelessness, anger, or empty feeling wey last about two weeks or more;
